WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.420
Last time I was outside this pub with Norm,

00:00:02.420 --> 00:00:04.080
he taught me how to strangle someone.

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:06.960
And now, he is going to teach me how to break someone's neck. Norm, it's all yours.

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:12.240
Right, so the key to doing a stage fighting
'snapping of the neck' is --

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:14.780
much like the previous type --

00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:19.060
is the person who's doing the snapping
doesn't do anything.

00:00:19.060 --> 00:00:21.560
-- Okay.
-- So I'm going to snap your neck

00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:23.100
-- Yep.
-- You are in control.

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:25.100
And you do absolutely nothing?

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:28.540
Well, I'll do ever so... 
but I'm not actually going to snap your neck(!)

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:33.560
It goes without saying that if you do this with someone you don't trust implicitly to do stage fighting...

00:00:33.560 --> 00:00:36.200
It's dangerous. Be careful.

00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:38.000
Norm, what are you going to do?

00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:40.900
First thing I'm going to do is put my hand on your chin.

00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:41.800
Okay.

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:45.080
And then adopt a "I'm going to snap your neck" pose.

00:00:45.080 --> 00:00:45.860
Yep.

00:00:45.860 --> 00:00:49.520
And then I'm just going to slightly pressure your chin.

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:51.520
Not enough to cause your face to move

00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:53.700
but so that you know my hand is there.

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:56.500
And when you're ready, snap your own neck.

00:00:56.500 --> 00:00:59.160
Okay. What, just as far as I can go?

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:01.760
Yeah. And obviously, try and sell the "huaaah!"

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:04.140
Okay. And kind of a [choking] noise?

00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:05.000
-- Yeah.
-- Okay.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:09.240
...

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:13.480
...

00:01:13.480 --> 00:01:17.040
...

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:17.740
I'm over there...

00:01:26.460 --> 00:01:27.680
I hope that looked good!

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:31.200
I don't know why I'm doing this. It doesn't hurt!

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:33.200
I'm instinctively going like this!

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:35.580
If it does hurt, I'm really sorry.
It's not supposed to!

00:01:35.580 --> 00:01:37.580
And that is how you break someone's neck on stage.

00:01:37.580 --> 00:01:40.260
This is Norm, and that -- I haven't said this in ages! --

00:01:40.260 --> 00:01:41.840
is something you might not have known.

00:01:42.340 --> 00:01:44.340
